{
  "summary": "Waits for the active chain tip to be connected in addition to chainstate loading before returning from `MakeMining(wait_loaded=true)`. This prevents early callers of the mining interface from reaching validation checks that require a chain tip.",
  "problem": "On a first start with an empty datadir or when starting with `-reindex`/`-reindex-chainstate`, `Init.makeMining` returns as soon as the chainstate is loaded, before the genesis block is connected. An external mining client calling `Mining.checkBlock` during this startup window triggers an assertion failure in `TestBlockValidity()` that aborts the node.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description and commit message: \"A Mining.checkBlock call in this window reaches TestBlockValidity(), which asserts that the tip exists, and the node aborts.\"",
    "Author note: \"The crash can be reproduced on master using the functional test included in this PR.\""
  ],
